# pc.world -- K10 P-C: probe-loop iteration probe (independent adversary design).
# True hidden order: w0<w1<w2<w3<w4<w5<w6<w7<w8<w9>.
# Two gaps: u1=(w4,w5) omitted (truth w4<w5); u2=(w6,w7) omitted (truth w6<w7).
# Bridges span the gaps: (w3,w5),(w4,w6) for u1; (w5,w7),(w6,w8) for u2;
# (w4,w7) closes the only other would-be unconstrained pair. Jump: (w0,w9).
# Negative (w7,w6,0) kills the u2-reverse variant. NO negative constrains
# u1's reverse, so the u1-false variant (adding (w5,w4)) is training-consistent
# and survives the consequence filter (HYP_KEPT 3 with E*).
# PAIR listing order -> first-appearance ids: w5=0,w6=1,w4=2,w7=3,w3=4,w8=5,
# w0=6,w1=7,w2=8,w9=9. u1 is id-pair (0,2), truth REVERSED vs id order:
# probe (0,2) truth 0, E* predicts 0 -> E* survives -> probe loop ITERATES.
# Second probe (1,3)=(w6,w7) truth 1 -> E* eliminated -> commit.
ORDER 10 w0 w1 w2 w3 w4 w5 w6 w7 w8 w9
TRAIN 18
PAIR w5 w6 1
PAIR w4 w6 1
PAIR w5 w7 1
PAIR w3 w5 1
PAIR w6 w8 1
PAIR w4 w7 1
PAIR w0 w1 1
PAIR w1 w2 1
PAIR w2 w3 1
PAIR w3 w4 1
PAIR w7 w8 1
PAIR w8 w9 1
PAIR w0 w9 1
PAIR w7 w6 0
PAIR w1 w0 0
PAIR w3 w2 0
PAIR w9 w8 0
PAIR w2 w1 0
HELDOUT_A 6
PAIR w5 w4
PAIR w4 w5
PAIR w6 w7
PAIR w7 w6
PAIR w3 w6
PAIR w2 w8
HELDOUT_AY 6
PAIR w5 w4 0
PAIR w4 w5 1
PAIR w6 w7 1
PAIR w7 w6 0
PAIR w3 w6 1
PAIR w2 w8 1
HELDOUT_B 6
PAIR w4 w6
PAIR w5 w8
PAIR w0 w7
PAIR w9 w3
PAIR w1 w9
PAIR w8 w0
HELDOUT_BY 6
PAIR w4 w6 1
PAIR w5 w8 1
PAIR w0 w7 1
PAIR w9 w3 0
PAIR w1 w9 1
PAIR w8 w0 0
NATTR 10
ATTR w0 3 8 1
ATTR w1 7 2 9
ATTR w2 1 5 4
ATTR w3 9 0 7
ATTR w4 4 6 2
ATTR w5 0 9 5
ATTR w6 8 3 0
ATTR w7 2 7 8
ATTR w8 5 1 6
ATTR w9 6 4 3
PROBE_EXCEPT 0
